<h2>Asobi Review 1.0.7 (build 2265) <span class="when">Nov 16, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Behind-the-scenes improvements</b> for the studio's tracking of review rounds.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0.6 (build 2262) <span class="when">Nov 16, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Overlay comments stay with their shot.</b> On a movie cut into short shots, a comment no longer reads on over the next shots.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.5 (build 2254) <span class="when">Nov 14, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The Source chip names the source.</b> When a shot's source render is on screen, the control bar's Source chip says so, and its menu flips back to the preview.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.4 (build 2251) <span class="when">Nov 14, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Zooming in a review is steady.</b> The picture could jump back and forth after someone zoomed. Now only a zoom or pan a person makes moves the room; resizing your window never does.</li>
<li><b>Overlay shows comments over the picture.</b> The Subtitles button is now Overlay. When the host turns it on for everyone you see the review's notes, each shot's progress note and the agency's comments. At most three show at once: click +N more (or press ⇧U) to see everything on the shot. Its menu sets the text size and the position.</li>
<li><b>The control bar shows the cache and the source.</b> Cache shows how much of the clip is ready to play; click it for Wait for Cache and Clear Cache. Source says which picture you are looking at.</li>
<li><b>Exports are grouped by what comes out.</b> The File menu has Export PDF and Export Notes and Frames; the note report and notes as text, CSV or SRT are there.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.3 (build 2239) <span class="when">Nov 13, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Swap a clip for another version.</b> Right-click a clip in the playlist and choose Swap Version: its other versions beside it are listed newest first, or Choose a Version… picks any file. A file that doesn't look like a version of the clip asks before it goes in. Each version keeps its own notes and drawings.</li>
<li><b>Relinking a moved review finds it.</b> A review whose movie was moved into another folder lost every shot, even when you chose the right folder. It now finds the movie by itself. When it does need to ask, the window names what is missing and lets you pick the file as well as a folder.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.2 (build 2229) <span class="when">Nov 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Web links show where they are.</b> While a web link is being made, the line under the progress bar names the clip it is working on and the step: encoding the picture, packaging it for streaming, or uploading. The clip count is also right now; it used to read one ahead.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.1 (build 2226) <span class="when">Nov 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Push a grade to the room.</b> In a live review, expert reviewers can send their grade on a clip to everyone, or put it on every clip, from the new icon in the grade panel. Other reviewers ask the host, who can allow it once or for the rest of the review.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2215) <span class="when">Nov 10, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Clips the host removes leave your playlist too</b> during a live review, instead of staying on your screen.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
